Connections

Flags:
      --list-models             write the available models to stdout and exit
      --provider STRING         run on this provider without a profile, typesafe,
                                openrouter, berget, levanto or cloudflare. Overrides
                                ONESIE_PROVIDER and the default profile. Refused beside
                                --profile or ONESIE_PROFILE
      --profile STRING          the profile a run uses, from profiles.json in the config
                                dir. Overrides ONESIE_PROFILE and ONESIE_PROVIDER, and
                                otherwise the default profile runs, which onesie profile
                                use sets
  -m, --model STRING            model override
      --base-url STRING         api root override. Also ONESIE_BASE_URL
      --allow-http              send the request, and any API key, over a plain http
                                base URL to a host other than this machine. Without it
                                such a base URL exits 2 before any request

How they work together:
  onesie is a Unix filter over the System One API, served by typesafe, openrouter,
  berget, levanto or cloudflare. A profile in profiles.json holds a provider, a key in
  the OS keychain or file, and optionally a model and base URL or cloudflare account.
  onesie profile create stores one and onesie profile use makes it the default.

  --profile overrides ONESIE_PROFILE and ONESIE_PROVIDER. Otherwise the default profile
  runs. --provider runs without a profile and overrides ONESIE_PROVIDER and the default
  profile. It is refused beside --profile or ONESIE_PROFILE. ONESIE_PROVIDER beside
  ONESIE_PROFILE is also refused. With no profiles, typesafe runs directly. Provider
  keys come from TYPESAFE_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, BERGET_API_KEY, LEVANTO_API_KEY
  or CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN. A chosen profile's key and endpoint beat the environment.
  Provider variables beat the default profile. --base-url wins over a chosen profile,
  then ONESIE_BASE_URL, then the provider's base URL or account variable, then the
  default profile. On typesafe, ONESIE_BASE_URL beats TYPESAFE_BASE_URL. A key and
  endpoint resolve as a pair from their applicable source.

  On cloudflare an account comes from the profile, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID or a base URL
  holding it. --model overrides the chosen profile or request body.
  TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL applies when none names a model and beats the default profile's
  model. A custom base URL needs no key and sends none when none resolves. Plain HTTP to
  a host other than this machine needs --allow-http, which permits sending the request
  and any API key over it. Without that flag the run exits 2 before a request. A profile
  storing such a URL needs --allow-http on every run too.

  Create a connection:
    onesie profile create NAME --provider typesafe

